{"step_index":1084,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:36:59Z","thinking":"**Investigating graph radius implementations**\n\nMathlib already defines `SimpleGraph.radius`, `SimpleGraph.eccent`, `SimpleGraph.ediam`, `SimpleGraph.diam`, and relevant theorems. However, `GraphCalc.radius` uses `ballWithin` and `minUpTo`, which is a different definition. The relation between `ballWithin` and `dist` needs examination.\n\n\n**Connecting `ballWithin` with walks**\n\nThe definition of `ballWithin` is equivalent to the condition `G.dist v w ≤ k`.  A direct connection between walks and `ballWithin` is being sought, aiming to prove `(p : G.Walk v w) → w ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G p.length v`.\n\nThe structure of `Walk` suggests that `cons` appends edges. The `mem_ballWithin_succ_of_adj` lemma shows how to add an edge to the end of a walk. Considering how to add an edge to the BEGINNING might prove useful.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > scratch.lean\\nimport Mathlib\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\n\\n#check Walk.concat\\nEOF\\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch.lean\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Checking Walk.concat\"","toolSummary":"\"Check Walk.concat\""}}]}
