{"step_index":1118,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:38:14Z","thinking":"**Interpreting the Walk Lemma**\n\nThe provided lemma, `mem_ballWithin_of_walk_le`, establishes that if a walk exists from node *u* to node *v* with a length less than or equal to *k*, then *v* belongs to the ball of radius *k* centered at *u* within the graph *G*. This defines a sufficient condition for a node to be within a certain distance of another node in a graph. The next step is to consider how this relates to graph distance.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"grep -A 4 \\\"exists_path_of_dist\\\" /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/lean_project/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Metric.lean\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking exists_path_of_dist\"","toolSummary":"\"Check exists_path_of_dist\""}}]}
{"step_index":1119,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:38:17Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:38:17+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:38:17+02:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\nlemma Reachable.exists_path_of_dist (hr : G.Reachable u v) :\r\n    ∃ (p : G.Walk u v), p.IsPath ∧ p.length = G.dist u v := by\r\n  obtain ⟨p, h⟩ := hr.exists_walk_length_eq_dist\r\n  exact ⟨p, p.isPath_of_length_eq_dist h, h⟩\r\n\r\nlemma Connected.exists_path_of_dist (hconn : G.Connected) (u v : V) :\r\n    ∃ (p : G.Walk u v), p.IsPath ∧ p.length = G.dist u v := by\r\n  obtain ⟨p, h⟩ := hconn.exists_walk_length_eq_dist u v\r\n  exact ⟨p, p.isPath_of_length_eq_dist h, h⟩\r\n\r\n--\r\n  obtain ⟨s, _⟩ := p₂.reachable.exists_path_of_dist\r\n  let r := ru.append s |>.append rv\r\n  have : p₁.length = ru.length + p₂.length + rv.length := by simp [h]\r\n  have : r.length = ru.length + s.length + rv.length := by simp [r]\r\n  have := dist_le r\r\n\n"}
{"step_index":1120,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:38:17Z","thinking":"**Verifying `ballWithin` equivalence**\n\nThe goal is to verify the lemma connecting `ballWithin` and graph distance. The crucial premise is `hconn`, asserting graph connectedness. This connectedness implies a walk exists between any two vertices whose length equals the distance between them. Consequently, the lemma claims that a vertex `v` is within the `ballWithin` of radius `k` centered at `u` if and only if the distance between `u` and `v` is at most `k`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' >> scratch.lean\\n\\nlemma mem_ballWithin_of_dist_le {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n    (hconn : G.Connected) (u v : V) {k : ℕ} (hle : G.dist u v ≤ k) :\\n    v ∈ GraphCalc.ballWithin G k u := by\\n  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := hconn.exists_walk_length_eq_dist u v\\n  rw [← hp] at hle\\n  exact mem_ballWithin_of_walk_le G p hle\\nEOF\\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch.lean\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Testing mem_ballWithin_of_dist_le\"","toolSummary":"\"Test mem_ballWithin_of_dist_le\""}}]}
