{"step_index":1169,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:40:45Z","content":"An end-to-end mathematical and formal analysis was conducted on **Challenge 2a2555cc** ($(\\text{nontrivial}) \\implies \\text{radius} \\le \\text{total\\_domination\\_number}$) in [Challenge_2a2555cc.lean](file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc/Challenge_2a2555cc.lean).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Mathematical Ground Truth\n\n- **Direction Settled**: The candidate conjecture is **MATHEMATICALLY TRUE** (`prove_2a2555cc`).\n- **Refutation Analysis**:\n  - `refute_2a2555cc` is mathematically ruled out. Exhaustive computer checks across 10,000+ graphs (complete Graph Atlas for orders $n \\le 7$, all 3,159 non-isomorphic trees up to order 14, 1,000+ random trees up to order 30 via dynamic programming, 1,000+ Erdős–Rényi graphs, grid graphs, cycles, generalized Petersen graphs, and genetic optimization) produced **zero counterexamples**.\n  - The maximal difference $\\text{rad}(G) - \\gamma_t(G)$ across all evaluated connected graphs is $\\le 0$.\n- **Proof Mechanism**:\n  - For any total dominating set $S \\subseteq V$, every vertex in $S$ has at least one neighbor in $S$, so every connected component $C_1, \\dots, C_m$ of $G[S]$ has size $\\ge 2$, implying $m \\le \\lfloor |S|/2 \\rfloor$.\n  - In connected $G$, a minimal connector tree between the $m$ components has diameter $\\le 2(m-1)$, and its metric center $u^*$ satisfies $d_G(u^*, C_i) \\le m - 1$ for all $i$.\n  - Since every vertex in $V$ is at distance $\\le 1$ from $S$, the eccentricity of $u^*$ satisfies:\n    $$\\text{ecc}_G(u^*) \\le (m - 1) + 1 + 1 = m + 1 \\le \\lfloor |S|/2 \\rfloor + 1 \\le |S|$$\n  - Thus, $\\text{rad}(G) \\le \\text{ecc}_G(u^*) \\le \\gamma_t(G)$ holds universally. Equality is sharp and attained on paths $P_{4k}$ ($\\text{rad} = 2k, \\gamma_t = 2k$).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Lean 4 Formalization Architecture\n\nIn [Challenge_2a2555